      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $7$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $2$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${135}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =7\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{135}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =14\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =7\\sqrt{2}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
